# mysqladmin — real-world examples

Reference: <https://www.tecmint.com/mysqladmin-commands-for-database-administration-in-linux/>

## Set / change the root password

```sh
# Set initial root password
mysqladmin -u root password YOURNEWPASSWORD

# Change an existing root password
mysqladmin -u root -p123456 password 'xyz123'
```

## Check the server is running

```sh
mysqladmin -u root -p ping
# mysqld is alive

mysqladmin -u root -p version
```

## Current status and activity

```sh
mysqladmin -u root -p status
# Uptime: 606704  Threads: 2  Questions: 36003  Slow queries: 0 ...

mysqladmin -u root -p extended-status
mysqladmin -u root -p variables
mysqladmin -u root -p processlist
```

## Homelab: create and drop databases

```sh
mysqladmin -u root -p create homelab_inventory
mysqladmin -u root -p drop testdb
```

## Homelab: check the MariaDB instance on mediaserver

```sh
mysqladmin -h mediaserver -u david -p ping
mysqladmin -h mediaserver -u david -p processlist
```

| Subcommand      | What it does                       |
| --------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| ping            | check server is alive              |
| status          | uptime, threads, queries           |
| extended-status | full status variables              |
| variables       | server configuration variables     |
| processlist     | active client connections          |
| create / drop   | create or delete a database        |
| flush-privileges| reload the grant tables            |
